From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: The clock opens the notification center and the calendar.

As in Windows 11, a click on the clock opens the notification center over
the calendar (startui.dll's ArcticClockFlyoutToggle), and another click
closes them. Every notification the shell shows, a program's balloon or
toast, goes to the notification center too, where a click on it is the
program's as on the balloon; with Do not disturb on, it is only there.
A change of the time or of the time zone (WM_TIMECHANGE) shows on the
clock at once.
